From 515b9f0e4ea4da403c5ad86b969c2cd0f919d081 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elektrobit <info@elektrobit.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Nov 2025 17:15:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bitbake: lib: bb: fetch2: use BASENAME if available

When combining (PRE)MIRRORS with the downloadfilename option the wrong
filename is used in the mapped mirror URL. Instead of the original
filename, the filename from downloadfilename is used. Modify this
behaviour to use the original filename instead.

Without (PRE)MIRRORS:

    DEBUG: For url https://github.com/GROUP/PACKAGE/archive/refs/tags/TAG.tar.gz returning https://internal.proxy.url/github/GROUP/PACKAGE/archive/refs/tags/TAG.tar.gz

With (PRE)MIRRORS:

    DEBUG: For url https://github.com/GROUP/PACKAGE/archive/refs/tags/TAG.tar.gz;downloadfilename=PACKAGE-TAG.tar.gz returning https://internal.proxy.url/github/GROUP/PACKAGE/archive/refs/tags/PACKAGE-TAG.tar.gz;downloadfilename=PACKAGE-TAG.tar.gz

Note that the filename component of the URL in the second example is
"PACKAGE-TAG.tar.gz", rather than "TAG.tar.gz".

Signed-off-by: Elektrobit <info@elektrobit.com>
Upstream-status: Inappropriate [waiting on response from upstream regarding intended behaviour]
---
 bitbake/lib/bb/fetch2/__init__.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bitbake/lib/bb/fetch2/__init__.py b/bitbake/lib/bb/fetch2/__init__.py
index 5bf2c4b8..50f555f4 100644
--- a/bitbake/lib/bb/fetch2/__init__.py
+++ b/bitbake/lib/bb/fetch2/__init__.py
@@ -470,6 +470,8 @@ def uri_replace(ud, uri_find, uri_replace, replacements, d, mirrortarball=None):
                     # Kill parameters, they make no sense for mirror tarballs
                     uri_decoded[5] = {}
                     uri_find_decoded[5] = {}
+                elif "BASENAME" in replacements and ud.method.supports_checksum(ud):
+                    basename =  replacements["BASENAME"]
                 elif ud.localpath and ud.method.supports_checksum(ud):
                     basename = os.path.basename(ud.localpath)
                 if basename:
-- 
